    "path": "/contentPages/0",
    "raw": "by K'arn Hollowbeak, Avian scholar\nThere are many forms of Avian burial, and the method often comes from the last will and testament of the deceased. Some Avians choose to float off attached to large balloons, while others favour cremation. Many simply opt for burial, but it is only the most important Avians who end up interred in tombs.",
    "value": "翼族学者 卡恩·空喙 撰\n翼族葬仪形式多样，处理遗体的方式通常依据逝者遗嘱而定。部分翼族选择以大气层为归宿，亦有倾向火化者。多数人仅行土葬，然唯有最为显赫之翼族，方得安息于陵墓之中。"
  },
  {
    "op": "replace",
    "path": "/contentPages/1",
    "raw": "Our tombs are vast and many, and the Sunborn through the ages are said to rest in many of them. Of course, the locations of the Sunborn's corpses have never been disclosed due to potential looters, but any tomb one steps in could hold the body of a god. ",
    "value": "吾族陵墓规模宏大，数量众多，历代太阳之子亦长眠于其内。然为防范盗墓之辈，诸神遗骸的具体位置向不外泄，以至踏入任何一座陵墓，其中皆可能安卧着一位神祇。"
  },
  {
    "op": "replace",
    "path": "/contentPages/2",
    "raw": "It is strange to think that our deities lie entombed amongst mortals. Strange to think of our gods dying, and yet all that remains is Kluex. May he live forever.",
    "value": "思及吾等神明竟与凡夫同葬一穴，着实令人感到奇异。神明亦会逝去，此念同样奇异，而留存至今的，唯有克鲁西斯。愿其永世长存。"
